From ac2a0c63473b1ddac5fdc3d3b6fe80f3f0ac1493 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:54:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WinSystemGbm: the full range of the tunnel needs QS on every
 backend

The AVI InfoFrame of the Dolby Vision Standard tunnel says full range RGB,
which is not the default range of its CTA modes. CTA-861 lets a source say
so only to a display that declares QS in a video capability data block.
Native output already refused a display without QS on NVIDIA, whose driver
sends the default range there; amdgpu and i915 now refuse the tunnel there
as well (Hades' drm_dvbridge.h on Linux 7.3, drm_dvbridge_sink_takes()), so
Kodi says it before it asks, on every backend, with the code "range". Not
for Low-Latency, whose AVI InfoFrame says YCbCr in the limited range.

Of the 485 real EDIDs of the host test that advertise the Standard mode,
2 have no such block (2015 and 2019).
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
index 3ef937c..d0644f2 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
@@ -1303,11 +1303,15 @@ bool CWinSystemGbm::SupportsNativeDVOutput(bool anyMode) const
   // linux-9965, as amdgpu does: no more "driveredid" here for them. The code still comes from
   // the driver when it refuses for its EDID: DVBRIDGE::REFUSED::Code().)
   // (Hades: not for Low-Latency, whose AVI InfoFrame says YCbCr 4:2:2 in the limited range)
-  else if (!lowLatency && backend == CDVBridgeState::Backend::NVIDIA &&
-           !info->SupportsRGBQuantizationSelection())
+  // (Hades: on every backend: the AVI InfoFrame of the tunnel says full range RGB, which is not the
+  // default range of its CTA modes, and CTA-861 lets a source say so only to a display with QS.
+  // amdgpu and i915 refuse the tunnel there too since Linux 7.3 (drm_dvbridge_sink_takes() of
+  // drm_dvbridge.h); NVIDIA's driver sends the default range to such a display.)
+  else if (!lowLatency && !info->SupportsRGBQuantizationSelection())
   {
     code = "range";
-    reason = "the display cannot select the RGB range (VCDB QS), needed with NVIDIA";
+    reason = "the display cannot select the RGB range (no VCDB with QS), which the full range RGB "
+             "of the tunnel needs";
   }
   else if (!(lowLatency ? info->SupportsLowLatencyDolbyVision2160p60()
                           : info->SupportsStandardDolbyVision2160p60()) &&
-- 
